{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>This time my husband will be joined to me, etc.</b> Rashi explained that she called his name Levi on account of לִוָּהוּ, 'he accompanied me,' with the gifts of priesthood, whereas Scripture states that she called him Levi on account of 'this time my husband will be joined (יִלָּוֶה) to me.' And what seems close to me to say regarding this is that the spirit of YHWH spoke through the tongues of the Matriarchs. And what she said when giving birth to the firstborn son — 'for now my husband will love me' (Genesis 29:32) — the intention was because there was born the firstborn son who would serve the service of HaShem, blessed be He, for the service was among the firstborn. And therefore Isaac loved Esau because he was the firstborn and thought that he would be the one to perform the service, and Rebecca loved Jacob, for she saw in prophecy that through her the birthright would return to Jacob. So too Leah said, 'for now my husband will love me,' by means of the firstborn son, for the eternal covenant would rest upon the son of the hated wife, in order to bring about love for her — and thus Mahar'i[a] explained in parashat Ki Teitse at the verse 'and the firstborn shall belong to the hated wife' (Deuteronomy 21:16). But the Holy One, blessed be He, knew that in the end the birthright would depart from Reuben on account of his profaning his father's bed, and if so, she is still the hated one. This is what she said: 'for HaShem has heard that I am hated and has given me this one too' (Genesis 29:33) — and she did not say that this son would bring about love for any reason, until she bore Levi, whom HaShem called Levi on account of לִוָּהוּ, 'he accompanied me,' with the gifts of priesthood in place of the service of YHWH that would rest upon him. And by this cause 'my husband will be joined to me' and will love me, for from me is born this time that son upon whom the burden of the service of HaShem, blessed be He, will rest. And according to this, Rashi's explanation is reconciled with the plain sense of the verse."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:31:14.648776317Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}